Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 14:14:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/31] chore(verimark): clean up logging for upstream review
 (Phase 10.4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Demote routine driver progress to fp_dbg / fp_info per upstream
convention :

  fp_warn  — actual recoverable errors (TLS handshake fail, missing
             sub1, file I/O fail)
  fp_info  — vfunc-level milestones (verify MATCH_SUCCESS / MATCH_FAIL /
             MATCH_ERROR, enroll progress milestones, bootstrap
             SUCCESS, stale-state recovery success)
  fp_dbg   — per-opcode / per-poll / per-swipe traces, "bootstrap
             skipped" notices

Remove the `g_print(">>> …<<<")` user-prompts in verify/enroll. Those
were daemon-stdout testing artifacts from the standalone standalone test harnesses
harnesses ; in fprintd context they pollute the journal and add no
value over the fp_info equivalents.

Rename `verimark_run_verify_pipeline` → `verimark_run_capture_match_pipeline`
(serves both verify and identify ; original name misled).

No behaviour change.
